{#
  Loading the site's typefaces. How they load is a site concern; what they are
  called is a theme concern, and the two are kept apart so a band can bring
  fonts from any provider without touching core.

  Adobe kit ids are tied to one Creative Cloud subscription and are
  domain-restricted, which is exactly why they live in site.json rather than
  here.

  Order matters, and not obviously: the first kit is loaded render-blocking and
  every other one is deferred behind media="print". So the kit holding the
  faces the page actually renders has to be first, or the text waits on a
  stylesheet that was deliberately taken off the critical path.

  This site had it backwards for a while. The blocking kit declared
  ballinger-mono at font-display:auto plus two families nothing referenced,
  while the deferred one declared both real faces at font-display:swap — so the
  swap never applied to first paint and fatfrank, which is every heading,
  arrived late. Check what a kit actually contains before adding a second one:

      curl -s https://use.typekit.net/<kitId>.css -H 'Referer: <your domain>'
#}
{% if site.fonts.provider == "adobe" %}
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://use.typekit.net" crossorigin>
  {% for kitId in site.fonts.adobe.kitIds %}
    {% if loop.first %}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://use.typekit.net/{{ kitId }}.css">
    {% else %}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://use.typekit.net/{{ kitId }}.css" media="print" onload="this.media='all'">
  <noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://use.typekit.net/{{ kitId }}.css"></noscript>
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
{% elif site.fonts.provider == "google" %}
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?{{ site.fonts.google.query }}&display=swap">
{% endif %}
